LICENCES — this release is split, because the parts differ in what they derive from.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CC BY 4.0   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  In the data release (HuggingFace):
  human_eval/        annotation sheets, ratings, derived results
  metadata/          datasheet, Croissant record, prompt manifest

  In the code release (GitHub):
  src/               profile generator, embedding generator, benchmark harness
  scripts/           every run script behind the paper
  tools/             verifier, split rebuilder, figure and table generators
  results/           per-seed result files produced by the harness
  manifest/          SHA-256 records
  paper/             the generated macro files the paper's numbers come from
  docs/              datasheet, reproducibility guide, protocol, surveys

These are our own work end to end. Nothing in them derives from a third-party
source, so they carry no upstream restriction and are offered under the most
permissive terms we can grant, commercial use included.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CC BY-NC 4.0   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  profiles/          LLM-generated item profiles, mood vectors, key themes
  embeddings/        encodings of that generated text, and composites of them

The text in profiles/ was written by a language model that was shown TMDb
metadata and MovieLens tag-genome scores. It is our output, but it is generated
FROM sources whose own terms are non-commercial, and we cannot grant rights we
do not hold. The non-commercial condition therefore reflects the upstream
position, not a preference of ours. Research use is unrestricted: academic and
industry researchers alike may use these files for research.

If you want these artifacts for a commercial purpose, contact the authors —
this restriction can be revisited if the upstream permissions widen.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NOT COVERED — not redistributed here, and not ours to licence
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  MovieLens 20M interaction data, tag genome, genre strings
      (c) GroupLens Research, University of Minnesota.
      https://grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/20m/ — obtain under their terms.
      No permission from GroupLens is required for this release, because none
      of their data is redistributed in it. Rebuild the benchmark splits with
      rebuild_splits.py from your own copy.
  TMDb metadata — obtain with your own API key.
  Open Library records used for the book catalogue (CC0).

ATTRIBUTION
Cite the accompanying paper. This product uses the TMDB API but is not
endorsed, certified, or otherwise approved by TMDB.
